  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPLEMENTING THE ARGENTINE SHOREBIRD CON</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Argentine Shorebird Conservation Plan provides a national framework to guide the efforts of public and private institutions, academia and civil society, and seeks to increase and strengthen the collective capacity for action to conserve shorebirds, at the national, provincial and local levels. This project represents the first part of its implementation and has five main components: 1) Strengthen baseline information on species and habitats at priority sites to inform and measure the effectiveness of management; 2) Develop and implement new mechanisms for recognition and protection of priority sites; 3) Safeguard and manage critical habitats through the implementation of collaborative solutions at the site scale; 4) Build capacity and agreements for good governance in site management and 5) Raise awareness and involve communities in conservation processes. This first phase of the Plan implementation will be piloted in five key shorebird sites: Punta Rasa, Albfera Mar Chiquita, Laguna Llancanelo, Laguna de los Pozuelos and Ansenuza.</narrative>
  </description>
